.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH switchboard 1  "switchboard 0.1.0" 
.SH NAME
switchboard \- Rust\-first local automation plane
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBswitchboard\fR [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Rust\-first local automation plane
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<PATH>\fR

.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
switchboard\-ns(1)
.TP
switchboard\-tools(1)
.TP
switchboard\-audit(1)
.TP
switchboard\-op(1)
.SH EXTRA
Raw CLI Coverage:
  Curated tools are the nice typed layer, not the limit.
  By default, any discovered provider CLI command can run through these raw surfaces:
    <provider>.cli.read   for read\-only commands
    <provider>.cli.write  for write commands
  Namespace auth, policy, approval, audit, and undo metadata still apply.
  Put switchboard flags before \-\-, then pass native CLI argv after \-\-.

Examples:
  switchboard ns list
  switchboard tools list
  switchboard tools describe google.cli.write
  switchboard tools describe github.cli.read
  switchboard audit list
  switchboard op list
  switchboard op list \-\-pending
  switchboard github.notifications.list \-\-ns github.personal \-\-json
  switchboard google.mail.search \-\-ns google.work \-\-query \*(Aqfrom:finance newer_than:7d\*(Aq
  switchboard google.calendar.list \-\-ns google.work \-\-ns google.personal \-\-json
  switchboard google.cli.read \-\-ns google.work \-\-json \-\- calendar +agenda \-\-format json \-\-today
  switchboard github.cli.write \-\-ns github.personal \-\- \-\-repo owner/repo issue comment 123 \-\-body \*(Aqneeds tests\*(Aq
  switchboard github.pull_request.comment \-\-ns github.personal \-\-repo owner/repo \-\-number 123 \-\-body \*(Aqneeds tests\*(Aq \-\-draft
  switchboard op approve op_1234abcd \-\-actor codex \-\-note \*(Aqship it\*(Aq
  switchboard op approve op_1234abcd \-\-actor codex \-\-apply \-\-json
  switchboard op undo op_1234abcd \-\-apply \-\-json
  switchboard op apply op_1234abcd \-\-json
.SH VERSION
v0.1.0
